WEBVTT

NOTE Timed from word timestamps of Narration_recorded.mp3 (video time = audio time + 0.4 s). Check by ear before release.

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.230
Meet Amina, a fictional farmer.

00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:05.710
She has a small plot, and the rains will soon decide her season.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.230
Before she plants, she must answer a question that sounds simple:

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:10.790
where will her seed come from?

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.550
Seed can reach her by many routes.

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:15.590
She might keep some from her own harvest.

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:16.970
She might ask a neighbour.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:18.690
She might buy at the local market,

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.810
join a cooperative that multiplies seed,

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.170
or visit a company's shop.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.030
Each route can meet different needs.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.810
Saved seed is close at hand and needs little cash.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.570
A neighbour may share a variety known to do well nearby.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:31.770
The market stays open when she is ready.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.910
A cooperative may offer quality information.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:35.850
A company may offer labelled seed,

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:37.750
though cash and travel can get in the way.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:40.570
No route is best for every farmer, or every season.

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:43.030
When cash is short, saved seed may fit.

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:45.290
When the rains are late, the market may help.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:48.730
When the crop is a hybrid, saved seed will not repeat its performance,

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.310
so fresh seed is needed.

00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:52.650
Behind her choice sit eight sector functions:

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:55.090
production, value addition and distribution,

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.210
service provision, utilisation,

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:59.590
stakeholder organisation, regulation,

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:01.370
coordination and financing.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:03.370
Together they shape what seed exists,

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:05.750
who can reach it, and what risk she carries.

00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:07.930
Notice whose voice is missing from this story.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.350
Who else chooses, shares or sells seed?

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:11.490
Who carries the cost?

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.010
Now try it yourself with three fictional farmers,

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:15.630
and see why the answer changes.

